        openings: ("Two bike patrol officers watched {D} hand a small item to a man at a park bench at 3:40 p.m. and take cash, and a search found nine baggies of methamphetamine, 3.1 grams in all, and $140, and {DL} had been before this court in {PRIORDATE} over {PRIOR}.", "The defense will say the baggies were for personal use and the cash was pay for a day's work. {D} did not sell anything to anyone."),
        closings: ("The officers saw a small item handed over for cash, nine baggies and $140 were found on {D}, and after {PRIOR} {DL} understood exactly what that means.", "A small item for cash can be anything, and a user carries baggies. The State must prove {D} sold methamphetamine, and nine small baggies fit the habit of a user as well as a seller."),
