        openings: ("{V} received three text messages between 11 p.m. and 11:40 p.m. from a number registered to {D}, and the messages said {D} knew where {V} parked after work, and {DL} had stood in this court in {PRIORDATE} over {PRIOR}.", "The defense will say {D} was drinking and never meant any harm, and sent texts a sober person would not send. {D} did nothing further."),
        closings: ("Three texts in forty minutes said {D} knew where {V} parked, they came from {D}'s number, and with {PRIOR} behind {D.him}, {DL} knew how {V} would take them.", "Drunken texts are foolish, not a plan to hurt, and {D} never came near {V}. The State must prove {D} intended {V} to be frightened, and three drunken texts with no follow-up do not show that."),
